    "prompt": "Below is a description of the Python function `BaseRequest.post`.\n\nDescription:\n\"\"\"\nThe `post` function in the `BaseRequest` class is an asynchronous method designed to parse and return the POST data from an HTTP request. It first checks if the POST data has already been parsed and cached in `_post`. If not, it verifies that the request method is one of the allowed POST methods and that the content type is either empty, `application/x-www-form-urlencoded`, or `multipart/form-data`. If the content type is `multipart/form-data`, it processes the request as a multipart form, reading each part, handling files by storing them in temporary files, and decoding text fields. For other content types, it reads the request body, decodes it, and parses it into a query string. The function returns a `MultiDictProxy` containing the parsed POST data. It handles errors such as unsupported media types and request entity too large by raising appropriate exceptions. The function relies on helper methods like `multipart()`, `read()`, and `parse_qsl()`, and uses the event loop to perform file operations asynchronously.\n\"\"\"\n\nSplit the description into atomic claims. Each claim must be a single, self-contained factual statement about the function that could be checked against the function's source code (name the function explicitly; no pronouns referring to other claims). Do not add claims that are not in the description; do not merge two facts into one claim. Keep the original wording where possible. Assign each claim exactly one type:\n- \"structural\": the function's signature, parameter names/defaults/types, return type, or which functions, methods, classes or attributes it uses.\n- \"dataflow\": how a value is computed, transformed, passed on, or what is returned for which input.\n- \"behavioural\": exceptions raised or caught, conditions/early returns, side effects, edge-case handling, ordering/iteration behaviour.\n- \"intent\": purpose, rationale, or the role of the function in the larger system.\n\nReturn a JSON array of at most 12 objects: [{\"text\": \"...\", \"type\": \"structural|dataflow|behavioural|intent\"}, ...]",
